  "notes": "パクる is slang that may come from the onomatopoeia パクパク (munching/gobbling sound), suggesting \"gobbling up\" something. It's also sometimes written as ぱくる in hiragana.\n\nREGISTER:\nThis is casual slang. Avoid using it in formal situations. For sense 1, use {盗|ぬす}む. For sense 2, use {盗作|とうさく}する or {模倣|もほう}する.\n\nRELATED NOUN:\nパクリ means \"a rip-off\" or \"plagiarism\" (noun form).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ～をパクる: to steal/copy something\n- ～からパクる: to steal/copy from someone",
